# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
poetry.toml

# Testing / tooling
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# DocKG local index -- reproducible from docs/ via `dockg build`.  Granular
# rather than a blanket `.dockg/`, matching doc_kg's own .gitignore: a bare
# `**/.dockg/` would also swallow `.dockg/snapshots/`, which is meant to stay
# tracked if this repo ever starts committing snapshots.
**/.dockg/lancedb/
**/.dockg/lancedb-*
**/.dockg/*.sqlite
**/.dockg/*.sqlite-shm
**/.dockg/*.sqlite-wal
**/.dockg/*.db
**/.dockg/models
**/.dockg/embeddings.json

# Rendered output.  The committed set lives at the top level in gallery/ --
# it is the presented work, not a build artefact, and burying it under
# renders/ made it look like one.  Everything under renders/ is output:
# quilts (25-40 MB each) are release assets rendered by
# .github/workflows/release.yml, and stills/ and views/ are local scratch --
# stills/ is where a working render goes while you are looking at it, and
# nothing there is expected to survive.  Promote to gallery/ only what earns
# a place in the documented set.
renders/*
!renders/README.md
# Run reports are the provenance record for renders whose output is *not*
# committed -- a quilt is a 25-40 MB release asset, its report is 2 kB of
# text saying which scene, commit, camera and POV-Ray made it. Ignoring
# these would leave the quilts unaccounted for.
!renders/reports/
# Quilts are never committed -- one 16" landscape quilt is 25-40 MB.  These
# two patterns have no slash, so git applies them at every depth: a quilt is
# ignored wherever it is written, not just under renders/.  Overriding that
# needs an explicit negation, which is deliberate.
*_qs[0-9]*x[0-9]*a*.png
*_qs[0-9]*x[0-9]*a*.mp4
pov-scenes/**/*.png

# PyMOL cartoon geometry.  Generated by quiltwright.pymol, and large -- one
# porin trimer is 8.9 MB -- so the four-line wrapper scenes are committed and
# the geometry is regenerated.  pov-scenes/vitrine/README.md has the command.
pov-scenes/**/*_cartoon.inc

# OS droppings.  None of these carry a slash, so git applies them at every
# depth -- a .DS_Store is ignored wherever the Finder leaves one, which is
# anywhere the tree has been browsed.
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd
._*
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor scratch.  .vscode/ is deliberately absent: settings.json is tracked.
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/

# Cruft
*.o

commit.txt

# POV-Ray resume state.  Written next to the output whenever a render is
# interrupted or run with +C, consumed when the render completes -- so an
# interrupted still leaves a multi-megabyte binary sitting where the image
# should be.  One of these reached the committed stills at 16.5 MB.
*.pov-state

# Personal working material -- grant drafts, venue correspondence.
# This is a public repository; nothing under grants/ belongs in it.
grants/
.pycodekg/graph.sqlite
.pycodekg/vectors.sqlite
docs/quiltwright_brand.md
